-- BrandDesk, the production wing: BUILD RECORD 1 (2026-11-01). Playbook branddesk-production-wing.
insert into playbook_records (slug, brand_slug, author, kind, source, body)
select 'branddesk-production-wing','lesaruss','Logan','decision','text', $br$BUILD RECORD 1, 2026-11-01 (Logan). Where BrandDesk stands at the end of 2026-11-01, and what comes next.

1. THE PARTNER CHECKOUT, LIVE (Sean: "Logan, build it", then "deploy"). vegansexplore-com main 0b3320a, ve-claims version 44, source sha256 matched. partnerTerms() is the shared calendar: 111-day periods from 2027-01-01 Eastern (P1 Jan 1 to Apr 21, 2027; P2 Apr 22 to Aug 10; P3 Aug 11 to Nov 29; P4 Nov 30 to Mar 19, 2028). Days 1 to 90 prorated at $1 a day left; days 91 to 111 the Preparation window, full $111 for the next period. Front Row Start charges $111 at sign-up, the days before Jan 1 are bonus. Stripe: a one-time line for what is due now, plus $111 every 111 days (interval day x 111) on a trial to the next shared renewal at noon Eastern; metadata.offer front_row | prorated | preparation, metadata.period. Public action partner_terms (at previews a date). Proven in Stripe test mode on Love Life Cafe with the QA account ($111 today, recurring $0 today, trial to Apr 22, 2027), then expired and removed. The Partner wording on /claim, /business, the listing page and brand tour, the business dashboard, the Restaurant Guide, the sample business, Preview journeys and /policies#business says periods; outreach Day 4 lost "No charge today" (migration 20261101_partner_periods_outreach_day4.sql). No one held the old no-charge trial.

2. PICTURE AND VOICE, NO VIDEO (Sean: "let's do picture and voice, no video"). The three lines that said the old terms are the Guide's voice over her still: Liz's offer on /claim (media/liz/partner-tour/j-5-v2.mp3), Maya's last brand tour slide (media/brand-door/front-row-v2.mp3, plain-last-v2.mp3, plain-last-first-v2.mp3). Recorded with el-media tts in their profile voices from the database (pg_net), each checked word for word with stt.

3. THE STUDIO IS BRANDDESK IN HQ, LIVE (Sean: "go", then "deploy"). lesaruss-hq main 4ed90c1: app/(shell)/studio moved to app/(shell)/branddesk, nav, links, staff routes and labels; /studio and /studio/* redirect (next.config.ts, not permanent); /api/studio data routes unchanged. Checked from the database (pg_net): old addresses land on the new ones, signed out asks to sign in.

4. THE SOCIAL ROOM, BUILT, NOT YET LIVE (Sean: "go", each brand's page is its home, starting with Social). Server half live: ve-social version 8 (vegansexplore-com 40e855c, sha256 matched) takes the admin token with as_member and acts as that person (their name on approvals and notes, their role). HQ half on lesaruss-hq branch claude/festive-cori-cvqs2o, commit b6653c1, NOT merged to main: lib/social.ts (memberIdForEmail, socialCall, SOCIAL_ACTIONS brands, slots, slot_get, approve, skip, send_back, note_add, report), app/api/branddesk/social/route.ts (signed in, staff, mapped to a members row, action whitelisted, as_member never taken from the client), components/branddesk/SocialRoom.tsx (Coming up / Posted and past by Eastern day, a sliding row a day, one post on its own with its media in the post's shape, caption, links, results, Approve and schedule, Skip it, Leave a note, Ask for changes, ?slot= in the address), and a Social tab in app/(shell)/branddesk/profile/ProfileClient.tsx. tsc clean, 122 of 122 tests. Tested against live data as contact@lesaruss.com (super admin): three brands, 10 posts in two weeks, a full post; a made-up member refused, a non-admin refused. Nothing approved (that pushes to Metricool). Editing media and captions links out to Depot > Social for now.

5. OPEN: WHICH ACCOUNT SEAN USES IN HQ. Sean (2026-11-01): "I sign in with contact@vegansexplore.com." The database has no auth user and no members row for that address. HQ signs in through Supabase auth: contact@lesaruss.com (super admin, last HQ sign-in 2026-10-31) and srussell@lesaruss.com (not a super admin, no Social role). The Social room needs a members row; with none it answers no_member. Logan's default: confirm the address Sean actually lands on in HQ before deploying; if it is contact@lesaruss.com nothing changes; if it is another, link it to the super admin members row rather than making a second account.

6. NEXT, IN ORDER. a) Settle 5, then "deploy" merges b6653c1 to HQ main; check it live (pg_net for the routes; Sean opens BrandDesk > a brand > Social). b) The foundation: the brand kit (business/brand.html, ve-brand-kit) inside BrandDesk with the mood board, the lock and the launch gate. c) The Website module (business/site.html, the frame). d) The plan engine. e) Run it on Sean A. Russell, GeekFon Society, Vegans Explore; then Green Leaf Kitchen; then the first client. Pitch deck is the first new wizard. Depot pages keep working until each has a home in BrandDesk.

Working notes: token-bearing calls (el-media, ve-function-deploy, ve-social tests) go through SQL net.http_post reading lesaruss_secrets, never the shell. Deploy an edge function from a commit with ve-function-deploy {slug, sha} and compare the source sha256. hq.lesaruss.ai and Vercel are unreachable from the build session; check from the database with net.http_get.$br$
where not exists (select 1 from playbook_records where slug='branddesk-production-wing' and body like 'BUILD RECORD 1, 2026-11-01%');
